; PineTree — 3rd Forest tree pick, added 2026-08-16 (Terrain look-pass follow-up). Human
; complaint: "It does not seem like forest cycles between multiple assets." The code was
; already alternating correctly (pick_variant()'s hash is even, forest.tres already wired
; both CommonTree1 and CommonTree2) — the real problem was that both existing "common
; tree" picks came from the same MegaKit set at the same ~2.5-tile canopy height and read
; as visually indistinguishable at the fixed ~45 camera pitch. This is a GENUINELY
; DIFFERENT silhouette (a narrow, tapered conifer, not another round-canopy "common tree"),
; not a third common-tree variant.
;
; Source: "Pine Tree" by Quaternius, CC0 1.0 Universal — poly.pizza (fresh individual
; download, 2026-08-16; no local MegaKit Pine/Twisted or Nature Pack Birch/Willow/Palm
; file was present on disk to hand-carry, matching the same "no local vendor/pack
; directory" situation the rest of this pass's poly.pizza sourcing already documents). CC0
; + Quaternius creator confirmed on the model page (poly.pizza/m/gX8WmgkeEm) before
; download, per asset-import-pipeline.md's audit gate. Recorded in
; project/attribution/sources/quaternius_poly_pizza_nature.tres.
;
; SCALE: the source file bakes a 90-degree axis correction + scale=100 into its own child
; node (Blender Z-up -> glTF Y-up), measured post-correction global AABB height = 3.565
; units (footprint ~1.26 x 1.37 at that height) — scaled here by 0.701 to hit the SAME
; ~2.5-tile canopy-height target CommonTree1/CommonTree2 use, so height stays a control
; variable and the silhouette/shape is the only thing that changes between variants. FIRST-
; PASS PROPOSAL, not a measured GDD number (none exists for tree height) — FLAG FOR HUMAN
; SIGN-OFF, including whether a pine reading TALLER/NARROWER than the common trees (rather
; than matched-height) would sell the "different tree" read even harder — that's a real
; alternative, left to the human's eyeball call rather than assumed here.
;
; SLAB IS 1.0x0.2x1.0 FROM THE START (not 0.94): this scene is new as of the SAME pass that
; widened every other terrain slab to close the cross-tile seam gap (see CommonTree1.tscn's
; header, "SLAB WIDENED 0.94 -> 1.0") — built at the corrected size directly rather than
; needing a follow-up fix.
;
; FLOOR TREATMENT MATCHES COMMONTREE1/COMMONTREE2 EXACTLY (same slab tint, same 3-patch
; moss/litter blotch treatment, same relative transforms) so a Forest tile's floor reads
; identically regardless of which of the 3 trees it lands on — same reasoning as
; CommonTree2's parity pass.
;
; EVERYTHING NESTED UNDER ONE NODE NAMED "Slab" (required, not cosmetic): identical
; OcclusionFader exemption requirement as CommonTree1.tscn/CommonTree2.tscn — see either
; scene's header for the full mechanism. The ground plane (renamed "Ground") and all 3
; floor patches are children of a wrapper Node3D literally named "Slab".
[gd_scene load_steps=8 format=3]

